                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course introduces undergraduates to cutting-edge interdisciplinary innovations in ophthalmology, covering AI-assisted diagnosis, biomaterials, surgical robotics, and advanced optical imaging. Through lectures, case studies, and hands-on projects, students will explore how engineering technologies transform ophthalmic diagnostics and treatments. Jointly taught by clinicians and engineers, the course aims to foster interdisciplinary thinking and practical problem-solving skills, preparing students for future careers in ophthalmic research or medical technology development.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
